The files are unmodified except for the local changes below.

Local changes
-------------

Each change is marked with an "illumos:" comment.  Each treats data the
device or firmware writes as untrusted where the upstream code does not.

    ctrl.c
	irdma_sc_ccq_get_cqe_info(): take the CQP from the device structure
	instead of the pointer in the completion entry, and reject an entry
	that names another; reject a WQE index at or above the SQ size before
	it indexes the scratch array and the SQ.
	irdma_sc_parse_fpm_query_buf(): return the result of
	irdma_osdep_fpm_query_check(), which bounds the FPM counts, sizes,
	block sizes and SD count before irdma_cfg_fpm_val() computes with
	them in the same function.
	irdma_sc_cfg_iw_fpm(): after parsing the commit buffer, return the
	result of irdma_osdep_fpm_commit_check(), which requires every
	committed object to lie inside the SD table before it is allocated
	and indexed.
	irdma_sc_process_ceq(): stop after one pass over the CEQ, so that
	entries with no registered CQ cannot keep the caller in the loop.

    uk.c
	irdma_uk_cq_poll_cmpl(): take the QP from irdma_osdep_cqe_qp(), which
	accepts the pointer and number in the CQE only if they name a live QP
	on this CQ, instead of dereferencing the pointer; drop entries that
	claim an SRQ; complete a send or receive only if its WQE index lies
	between the ring's tail and head; bound the walk over a flushed send
	queue by the ring size and treat a zero quanta count as one.
	irdma_uk_clean_cq(): stop after one pass over the CQ.

The checks themselves are in ../irdma_osdep.c.  Other untrusted values are
handled outside core/ without changes here: CEQ entries resolve only to CQs
registered on the CEQ (the driver passes reg_cq), AEQ completion contexts
are never dereferenced and AEQ QP and CQ numbers index bounded tables, and a
receive completion's length is checked against what was posted
(../irdma_cq.c).

usr/src/test/irdma-tests checks that each marker is present and that this
list matches them.

Re-import policy
----------------

1. Copy the files from one Linux commit without changes and record the
   commit and blob IDs above.  Check each license line first.
2. For each local change, check whether upstream now has an equivalent
   check; drop the change if so, otherwise apply it again with its
   "illumos:" comment.  Update this list.
3. Put OS glue in ../osdep.h and the driver, not here.
4. Run python3 -B usr/src/test/irdma-tests/run_tests.py and a full module
   build with smatch before the change is committed.
